-extends "channels/channel_claim_form.html"
-load i18n compress temba


-block pre-form
  -blocktrans trimmed with name=brand.name
    You can connect a <a href="https://core.telegram.org/bots">Telegram bot</a> to your {{ name}} workspace to
    automate sending and receiving Telegram messages.

  -blocktrans trimmed
    You'll need to <a href="https://core.telegram.org/bots#create-a-new-bot">create a new Telegram bot</a> and get its
    authentication token. To do so:

  %ol.steps.card
    %li
      -blocktrans trimmed
        Start a new chat with the <a href="https://telegram.me/botfather">BotFather</a> by searching for "botfather"
        on your device.

    %li
      -blocktrans trimmed
        In your @botfather chat, type the command <code>/newbot</code>. Follow the instructions to name your bot and
        choose a username.

    %li
      -blocktrans trimmed
        Once you've created your bot, @botfather will provide you with the authentication token. Enter that token
        below.
